<title>USA: Fidelity boosts analysts' pay 20-25 pct - Barron's.</title>
<headline>Fidelity boosts analysts' pay 20-25 pct - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mutual fund giant Fidelity Investments has quietly raised the salaries of its top senior analysts by as much as 20-25 percent in recent weeks to keep them from defecting to rival firms, Barron's reported.</p>
<p>The raises mean that, with performance perks, some senior analysts now make as much as $600,000 a year, even before stock bonuses, the magazine said, citing sources close to Fidelity.</p>
<p>The magazine said that William Hayes, head of Fidelity's equity department, confirmed that the raises had been given, although he would not comment on their size.</p>
</text>
